{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance","id":1548410,"title":"Running the Free States - 3 - Practical Governance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-11T16:23:01-08:00","id":1548410,"title":"Running the Free States - 3 - Practical Governance","content":"I am still working out some practical details on how to run the Free States. Even after reviewing Los Angeles By Night, Anarch Cookbook, Clanbook: Brujah and other sourcebooks, not everything is clear. I must make a lot of things up, so hearing some feedback is good.<br /> <br /> So the basis of governance in the Free States is the Status Prefectus, which is more a statement of principals than any guide to governance. To sum up the major points:<br /> <br /> 1 the Anarchs want to free themselves from any forces that rob them of their \u201cLibertas\u201d.<br /> <br /> 2 They owe no allegiance to any creature or organization<br /> <br /> 3 They will rule themselves with no ruler other than that they choose for themselves<br /> <br /> 4 They recognize their responsibility to maintain, protect, and defend the Masquerade<br /> <br /> 5 They declare their kinship and support of all Kindred still struggling for their own Libertas<br /> <br /> As long as any domain operates under the Status Perfectus, it is accepted as being part of the greater Anarch Free States themselves.<br /> <br /> = = =<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council\">Part 1 - the Anarch Council</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine\">Part 2 - Germaine</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs\">Part 4 - Canon Characters &amp; Gangs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites\">Part 5 - Setites</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549587-running-the-free-states-6-petrodon-and-the-camarilla\">Part 6 - the Camarilla</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club\">Part 7 - San Francisco</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat\">Part 8 - Sabbat</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements\">Part 9 - Crossovers</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552818-running-the-free-states-10-the-oddball-stuff\">Part 10 - Oddballs</a>\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  adding links 08-01-2025, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-11T16:28:37-08:00","id":1548411,"title":"","content":"There is also some practical information on how things actually work found in the sourcebook.<br /> <br /> Vampires stake out territories and forbid other vampires to hunt in them. So exclusive feeding territory is respected. These are the \u201cbaronies\u201d. Gangs are defined by their exclusive feeding territory, not where they live. Vampires can dwell or visit any place they want, but in terms of feeding, they can only do so in their gang\u2019s territory. The major exception is the so-called Barony of Angels which is controlled by Jeremy MacNeil and his buddies which is open to everyone (including other gangs).<br /> <br /> The Barony of Angels is not \u201cruled\u201d by any gang, including MacNeil\u2019s. He simply prevents anyone from claiming it. It is open hunting grounds unlike the other baronies, but Kindred are to be careful and clean up after themselves. Coteries are for companionship and self-protection only.<br /> <br /> The Barons and their gangs often destroy any Kindred who hunt in their area who are not given permission. The Crypt\u2019s Sons only gives permission to members of their gang. Other \u201cgangs\u201d are more permissive and allow non-members allies and possibly even others to feed.<br /> <br /> Violence between coteries/gangs is normal. The way to protect oneself is to belong to a powerful coterie/gang that deters or avenges others. I take this to mean that Kindred can destroy other Kindred as they see fit. The only thing stopping them is the fear of initiating a feud, or that they may provoke other Kindred to ally and gang up against them. In other words, nobody is protected from destruction in the sense that the Sixth Tradition reserves this exclusively to the Prince.<br /> <br /> It is explicitly mentioned that any Kindred can embrace whenever they want.<br /> <br /> So if we compare this to the Six Traditions, both abide by the Masquerade. There is a limited form of domain in the sense that feeding territory is exclusive. The traditions of progeny, accounting, and destruction are thrown out. Hospitality isn't addressed. I imagine that while there is no obligation to announce yourself upon arrival to the Free States, or if you enter a barony, those &quot;in charge&quot; will probably make themselves known when convenient.<br /> <br /> The issue of blood bonds is not addressed in LABN. There are characters who are blood bonded in the sourcebook, but I think it\u2019s supposed to be a secret. I cannot imagine the Free States would allow blood bonds at all. Although I do wonder if mutually agreed blood bonds between two Kindred in love would be tolerated. I am thinking blood bonding another vampire to you is probable justification for destruction by anyone who is willing to do it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-11T16:38:41-08:00","id":1548413,"title":"","content":"The closest thing to a legislature are the Rants. Anarch Rants (open to everyone, not just Brujah) are held every other full moon. Often a hundred Kindred attend. Venues changed as they become larger, but currently they are held in a huge abandoned bus terminal just north of Hollywood Boulevard. It is now a converted nightclub called the Terminal.<br /> <br /> Any speaker can speak for however long they want, but are usually limited by the jeers of the audience.<br /> <br /> Speakers can call for votes on topics, but are no more binding than the speaker wishes them to be (I think it means he will enforce any decisions himself which means he must be important).<br /> <br /> If topics require individual action, then the speaker either does it himself or asks for volunteers to do so.<br /> <br /> Rants usually (peacefully) decide any dispute between groups provided a speaker brings up the matter and brings it to the group\u2019s decision.<br /> <br /> Taken together, I believe they imply the following. 1) Rants can decide new &quot;policy&quot;, but subsequent rants can easily revoke or change such policies. 2) Anything decided must be enforced on a personal basis. There is no government to do so. Policies adopted at a Rant can only be enforced if the speaker is willing to do it or themselves, or other Kindred step up to do it alongside with her or in place of her. This effectively means that anything decided which is not enforced probably lapses fairly quickly. The main purpose of speaking at a Rant is to see first hand how popular your proposed action is, and who among the powerful could be opposed to it.<br /> <br /> The Rants do seem to cover ALL the baronies. It isn't limited to MacNeil's Barony of Angels. The other gang leaders do show up and participate. It's not clear if other Free States outside the immediate LA urban area is also covered. It's mentioned that Tara in San Diego used to regularly attend, but doesn't anymore. There are also other &quot;outlying&quot; baronies like Fresno and San Jose. I imagine most of those baronies effectively govern themselves and work out any problems between themselves. Unless they have ambitions, there's no real reason to travel to LA and bring up your issues because in the end, you can only rely on yourself and your coterie anyway.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T13:47:44-08:00","id":1548448,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll bet this whole set-up gives at least one European Kindred unhappy flashbacks to the liberum veto/golden freedom of the Polish Commonwealth - and quite a few US Kindred of a certain age happy memories of the often bare-knuckle politics of the American Frontier: I\u2019ll bet slinging accusations, insults and just about anything else that comes to mind at rivals has been raised to a High Art at these Free State Raves (Think the Congressional scenes from LINCOLN with the occasional deployment of claws).<br /> <br /> Honestly, in the Free States politics seems to be a Spector Sport (With or without kayfabe, I wonder?).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T19:57:45-08:00","id":1548457,"title":"","content":"I would compare Rants more to a viking thing since they both lack police to enforce the law (you have to enforce anything by yourself and by those who support you) except the Rant is even weaker. It seems to have no judicial powers at all. At best you can see if the Kindred there are mostly sympathetic to you so you can justify the action you take.<br /> <br /> It can probably serve as a forum for mediation and social pressure to compel two sides to come to an agreement, but only if the two sides aren't really willing to go to war.<br /> <br /> I also see it as a forum for &quot;alternative&quot;, more peaceful forms of competition when a decision is sought, but neither side wants violence and is willing to accept the &quot;authority&quot; of the rant. Similar to flyting, battle rap, or poetry slam. So it only really works if both sides are reasonable, relatively equal, and willing to accept a loss. One would be a fool to expect a more powerful Kindred to accept the loss in such a contest in a matter that is very important to her. But it could be an important way for Kindred to let off steam without things collapsing into violence.<br /> <br /> More powerful Kindred likely appeal to the real leaders of the Free States (the most powerful gang leaders/barons) for mediation and negotiation directly rather than appeal to the crowd although this is even more informal and personal.<br /> <br /> I expect for the powerful barons, the Rant's main importance is to build enough public support to justify violence that would ordinarily spark outrage, controversy, or other reaction that would otherwise allow for a backlash if not cloaked in support of the mob. Athenian democracy and mob rule at its worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-13T04:43:18-08:00","id":1548468,"title":"","content":"Heaven knows that there a plenty of precedents for a \u2018talking shop\u2019 legislature that can declare laws, but requires private individuals to put them to work - the Parliament of Great Britain <i>vis a vis</i> the London underworld during the 18th century, for instance.<br /> <br /> Heck, I\u2019d put money of Jeremy MacNeil\u2019s vision for the Anarch Free States having strong elements of the \u2018By mutual consent and force of arms, by individuals and not by institutions\u2019 approach of more than one polity from his breathing days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-13T08:22:22-08:00","id":1548471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance?p=1548457#post1548457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect for the powerful barons, the Rant's main importance is to build enough public support to justify violence that would ordinarily spark outrage, controversy, or other reaction that would otherwise allow for a backlash if not cloaked in support of the mob. Athenian democracy and mob rule at its worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that. Calling someone out at a Rant would allow you to see who supports who. If you get shouted down you know you would have a hell of a time if it came to violence. If you get the cheers, though, you know you can get away with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-13T14:45:45-08:00","id":1548483,"title":"","content":"Cool ideas Black Fox \ud83e\udd8a.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-14T05:45:40-08:00","id":1548493,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Practical Governance, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, May I please ask if you\u2019ve been able to put together a shortlist of the Barons across the Anarch Free States? <br /> <br /> I can recall The MacNeil* in \u2018The Barony of Angels\u2019, Tara Kierney in San Diego and Fortier up in the hills - also that there are (or were) Barons in San Jose &amp; Fresno, but one is aware that there are others I\u2019m forgetting.<br /> <br /> May I please ask if you can help me with this?<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>*I tend to imagine his most Caledonian-enthused followers talking about Jeremy MacNeil as though he were a Clan chief/the Chief of his name from the Old Highlands - he much prefers \u2018MacNeil\u2019 to his face, though he\u2019ll accept \u2018Jeremy\u2019 (He\u2019ll outright ignore anyone who calls him \u2018Jerry\u2019 and might even stoop to passive-aggressiveness) - also that some of the most over enthusiastic of his immediate following even tend to add \u2018MacNeil\u2019 to their own name as a token of their admiration.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, one assumes that \u2018Jeremy\u2019 is an anglicisation of his birth name (He probably went by \u2018Jeremiah MacNeil\u2019 back in the day, but my guess is that his original name was \u2018Diarmaid\u2019 in the Gaelic).<br /> <br /> Kilts aren\u2019t banned, but they\u2019re certainly frowned upon unless it\u2019s Burn\u2019s Night, Hogmanay or (At a pinch) Saint Andrew\u2019s Day (In my imagination Jeremy MacNeil retains a fine, Enlightenment disrespect for veneration of the saints and organised religion).<br /> <br /> <br /> </i>Incidentally, given that San Jose is \u2018Capital of Silicon Valley\u2019 and is, or was, the third richest city on Earth in terms of GDP per head (Not to mention is sited hard by San Francisco on the Golden Bay) I\u2019d bet that it\u2019s a key Zone of Contention between Anarchs &amp; Camarilla.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d bet the Camarilla are winning too, as they tend to when there\u2019s Serious Money on the table.<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, what research I\u2019ve been able to do suggests that - in addition to the Barons - California had or has Princes at \u2018East Bay\u2019 (Berkeley/Oakland), San Francisco (Naturally) and Whittier \u2026 although that one may actually be a Baron, this is what happens when you work from Rough Notes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-14T11:37:01-08:00","id":1548497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance?p=1548493#post1548493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Speaking of Practical Governance, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, May I please ask if you\u2019ve been able to put together a shortlist of the Barons across the Anarch Free States?</div> </div> </div> </div>If we go by LABN there's a lot because practically every suburb is controlled by a &quot;gang&quot;, and these little gangs are rarely given a leader's name.<br /> <br /> The other major official baronies are the Crypt's Sons in South Central LA, La Hermandad in East LA ruled by Salvador Garcia's band of anarchists, David Geduld's group in Torrance, Steve Booth's surfer bros in Long Beach, Amethyst's gang in Santa Ana, and two gangs fighting over Anaheim. Those are the main NPCs. The minor gangs in the direct LA area are usually allied to one of the larger gangs.<br /> <br /> For myself, I am keeping to only some of that. I'm consolidating some of the gangs, demoting others to just coteries, and adding new ones. I want what gangs exist to actually matter. I brainstormed some ideas on real competing politics among the anarchs and the roles of the different gangs <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them\">on this thread</a> from several years ago. So if you want some insight on how I might run the Free States, that should give you some idea. I think I started posting heavily around page 4 or 5 of that thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance?p=1548493#post1548493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, given that San Jose is \u2018Capital of Silicon Valley\u2019 and is, or was, the third richest city on Earth in terms of GDP per head (Not to mention is sited hard by San Francisco on the Golden Bay) I\u2019d bet that it\u2019s a key Zone of Contention between Anarchs &amp; Camarilla.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d bet the Camarilla are winning too, as they tend to when there\u2019s Serious Money on the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we should probably talk about San Jose and the Bay Area in general once I post a thread on San Francisco and what role it should play in an LA Free State chronicle. Officially it is like you say, an area of contention between the Camarilla and anarchs. The anarchs control it, but vampires from San Fran have tried to regain it from time to time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-18T13:31:19-08:00","id":1548567,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, I\u2019ve read through that thread and have some thoughts regarding your own notions for (and notion of) various characters.<br /> <br /> Might I please ask where you would prefer me to post those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-18T18:28:52-08:00","id":1548578,"title":"","content":"Go to the Canon Characters &amp; Gangs thread I started, link in the first post of this thread and others.<br /> <br /> In addition to the general rules of the Free States, that each &quot;gang&quot; controls their own feeding territory de facto allows each of them to create their own mini-domain with their own rules. Since the Status Perfectus allows for Kindred to &quot;rule themselves&quot; and have a ruler &quot;that they choose for themselves&quot;, I guess this is an out that each gang can justify as still following the status perfectus.<br /> <br /> I assume the larger and more powerful gangs have rules that members must follow, otherwise they get booted out of the gang and lose access to their feeding territory. Things like having an actual leader (no matter how determined), some type of internal hierarchy and command structure, and additional rules are all in place. They might even have rules that embracing new childer without authorization might get you kicked out. You can justify a lot by saying that &quot;gang&quot; membership is voluntary, and that anyone not accepted already has a home in MacNeil's Barony of Angels.<br /> <br /> The Crypt's Sons likely have strict rules since it is based on an existing gang structure. I imagine David Geduld's group also has some strict requirements. Even the anarchist La Hermandad probably has some internal rules because it comes out of a conspiratorial anarchist tradition, and secret societies tend to have things like sworn oaths and honor rules based on loyalty and commitment to the cause.<br /> <br /> I also intend to introduce some additional factions not found in LABN which likewise have their own membership requirements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-19T13:43:47-08:00","id":1548598,"title":"","content":"I look forward to meeting them! Preferably not in the lroverbial dark alley, though (Or a literal dark alley, for that matter).<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I wonder how often the Crypt\u2019s Sons are called \u2018The Crypts\u2019 plain and simple?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-19T19:21:08-07:00","id":1549455,"title":"","content":"How should diablerie be treated in the Free States? Even among anarchs I think the vast majority of the Kindred of the Free States would be appalled by it. Nobody likes the idea of cannibalism. The Anarch Cookbook mentions that even most anarchs are unwilling to do it. It is a foul and perverted act.<br /> <br /> While players often think of diablerie solely as the young and weak gaining power at the expense of the strong, it is important to remember Kindred cannibalism also works the other way. Ancient methusalehs devour their own childer, and there are stories of degenerate elders devouring their own childer or other weaker vampires. Drinking vitae of their fellow Kindred is extremely pleasurable to vampires, more than even drinking mortal blood. So even the weakest generation have reason to hate and fear it.<br /> <br /> Yet we know that there are a significant number of anarchs who do it. Some of these are just the normal criminal sort who gravitate to the anarchs for safety in numbers and cover, but there are also other types. Diablerie is a way for the anarchs to gain power and weaken the power of the elders. It is also a tactic used to demoralize and spread fear among their enemies.<br /> <br /> The Anarch Cookbook also mentions that some &quot;mystically inclined anarchs&quot; believe the world is a thought-construct of an ancient pre-Flood vampire (perhaps Caine), and that vitae is the only real connection to this true source of reality. By following that &quot;connection&quot; by improving one's generation through diablerie, the vampire can return to the &quot;real&quot; world. It's a religious excuse for diablerie, and supposedly is a popular rationale for some neonate anarchs who practice diablerie. It sounds very Malkavian to me. However, the Free States is exactly the kind of place that this kind of argument could be openly discussed and find adherents, and once a certain critical mass is achieved it would spread to anarchs in other domains.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea in Blood Hearts - Diablerie: Britain that some anarch diablerists find Das Buch vom Grabkrieg (actually Dr Mortius's translation of that book) fascinating because it gives an insight into the methusalehs, and that's important if they are to go hunting for them for the purposes of diablerie. (It also foretells the coming of the anarchs so it is popular for that as well.) That the book itself is restricted and most likely only known through barely legible photocopies of photocopies of translations (at least in the early nineties, things would be different now) makes it an excellent &quot;treasure&quot; for the PCs to stumble upon in the Free States.<br /> <br /> So I imagine there must be at least one open group of self-admitted diablerists, and probably even more secret ones. There are no laws against diablerie, but it remains unpopular. Self-admitted diablerists are probably fairly powerful and feared by many, but they run the risk of becoming hated and destroyed if the opponents of diablerie are provoked through a combination of anger and opportunity.<br /> <br /> I just like the idea of the PCs running into open diablerists who justify the practice and argue there is no shame to it. I want to include both the &quot;good&quot; side of the Free States and the &quot;bad&quot; side.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of at least two coteries who are open about it. The first presents the more &quot;practical&quot; side of diablerie - it's a good weapon to weaken their enemy. The second talks about it more mystically. There's several bad photocopies of Dr Mortius's translations, and there might be wars over someone trying to produce a more legible copy by getting all the copies and replacing illegible pages with more legible pages shown in someone else's copies. There is even one group (maybe of secret diablerists) planning a big raid on a methusaleh like shown in the Diablerie adventure books. (I am not interested in running such an adventure myself, but I could make reference to some coterie planning to go down to the Yucatan and then never heard from again.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-20T13:06:53-07:00","id":1549460,"title":"","content":"I suspect that the Free States\u2019 tendency to run along \u201cWe are all about freedom, including Freedom to take the consequences\u201d lines is never more pronounced than in it\u2019s attitude to the amaranth - for one thing, I\u2019d bet that anyone advocating \u2018Top-down\u2019 diablerie would have to do so very, very discretely or find themselves on the sharp end of an angry mob (Whether a lynch mob or <i>posse comitatus</i> I leave you your imagination.<br /> <br /> One also suspects that advocacy of diablerie for mystical and/or theological reasons would be greeted with considerable suspicion by those local Kindred with real knowledge of the Sabbat and it\u2019s core beliefs (In fact that coterie of more occult diablerists would almost certainly make a useful false lead if you want to keep Our Heroes from ferreting out the local talons on the Black Hand too quickly), though whether this represents a high proportion of LA Kindred (or even an influential portion) is an interesting question.<br /> <br /> Quite frankly, I tend to agree that the Anarch Free States would be more open to \u2018practical diablerie\u2019 in principle than in practice: as you have noted, nobody trusts a vampire who has swallowed another vampire\u2019s soul, even when they feel obliged to work with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-20T13:08:53-07:00","id":1549461,"title":"","content":"Oh, and I\u2019m simultaneously amused, fascinated and rather disturbed by the fact that the World of Darkness has produced a \u2018Gospel for Cannibal Vampires\u2019 - it\u2019s so very genuinely horrifying and yet so deliciously OTT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-20T22:02:58-07:00","id":1549473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance?p=1549460#post1549460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One also suspects that advocacy of diablerie for mystical and/or theological reasons would be greeted with considerable suspicion by those local Kindred with real knowledge of the Sabbat and it\u2019s core beliefs (In fact that coterie of more occult diablerists would almost certainly make a useful false lead if you want to keep Our Heroes from ferreting out the local talons on the Black Hand too quickly), though whether this represents a high proportion of LA Kindred (or even an influential portion) is an interesting question.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's mentioned in Clanbook Brujah 1e that some Kindred estimate that up to 10% of the Los Angeles vampire population is Sabbat. It's entirely possible part of that (unsupported) number includes known diablerists like these guys, and Petrodon or whoever thinks &quot;These guys must be Sabbat.&quot; Then again, Petrodon accuses Salvador Garcia of diablerie so he just may think that of everyone.<br /> <br /> The obvious Gnostic connotations of that &quot;mystical&quot; anarch idea of diablerie could be just a product of 20th century ideas, or it might be partially inspired by beliefs of the Cainite Heresy that were developed years later (in real time) in the Vampire: the Dark Ages line, or somehow based on Assamite teachings, or any number of other things. If I'm going to have such a group in the chronicle, I think it makes sense for them to be a way to introduce various oddball bits of lore and see if anything intrigues of the imagination of the PCs.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-21T12:32:58-07:00","id":1549488,"title":"","content":"That sounds like an excellent idea - if nothing else it shows how fine the line between the Factions can be, especially in a free for all situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-24T18:22:51-07:00","id":1549546,"title":"","content":"Another I'd like to talk about is the role of clan culture and clans in general in the Anarch Free States. The LABN sourcebook says there is a &quot;complete breakdown of the clan system that dominates the Camarilla.&quot; Many Kindred who arrive in the Free States have &quot;either rejected their clan or been rejected by it&quot;. The large coteries (gangs) have replaced most of the functions traditionally fulfilled by clans. Attempts by the Camarilla to divide the Free States by appealing to one's clan loyalty falls on deaf ears.<br /> <br /> I take this to mean that to a certain degree that the anarchs of the Free States see &quot;clans&quot; as a tool of the elders to keep the young divided and unable to resist elder rule. Why should it matter to a young neonate who was the progenitor of their bloodline? What loyalties should one owe solely that five to ten generations ago you and some other vampire had the same clan founder sire your line? There's some merit to this argument.<br /> <br /> Now of course, this does not mean clan identity is completely unimportant, just that it is a lot less than in Camarilla domains. We do know there are certain clans that are less &quot;popular&quot; or Kindred from them are (at least initially) less trusted than others. But what does this mean in practice, particularly for things like clan meetings and other defining features of that clan that should appear in a traditional Camarilla domain?<br /> <br /> I think there is little change for Brujah and Gangrel. Brujah clan culture, to a large degree, is the political culture of the Free States. Their system of Rants basically became the defining feature of Free States &quot;governance&quot;. The anarch rants are basically Brujah rants open to everyone. Gangrel are also not much impacted. Gangrel <i>things</i> aren't the same as Brujah <i>rants</i>, but Gangrel culture prizes the individual. And should Gangrel really need to discuss something among themselves, they probably meet in a wilderness place outside LA anyway.<br /> <br /> Malkavians are probably not affected either. First, I think other Kindred would just give up trying to stop them from meeting since its futile. Second, Malkavian clan meetings are already &quot;open&quot; to other Kindred. Malkavians in LA doing their own thing probably won't be seen as disloyal to the Free States. But what about the other clans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-24T18:24:06-07:00","id":1549547,"title":"","content":"Tremere in LA are probably already rare, but I think any that do dwell there would be advised to NOT meet and discuss &quot;clan business&quot;. Tremere &quot;clan business&quot; would be chantry type stuff, and any possible ties to the Tremere Pyramid would be considered hostile and treasonous by everyone else. I am not saying that Tremere in LA cannot or don't occasionally meet up with each other. Just that it is ill advised, and they probably work hard to stay away from each other. Even Tremere in a common coterie could be seen as suspicious.<br /> <br /> Likewise, I don't think the Ventrue meet up in a local board meeting. The Ventrue already possess a fairly high profile in the Free States that one would likely not guess before reading the sourcebook. Fortier is a prominent baron controlling West LA. David Geduld controls Long Beach. Even Salvador Garcia's right hand man, Jesus Ramirez, is a Ventrue, and he effectively rules La Hermandad when Garcia is away (which is often). Three major Ventrue barons probably strikes a lot of Brujah as bad. If they actually meet up like a clan, it'll raise alarm bells. For that reason, I think they don't meet, and if any new Ventrue show up and innocently ask where the clan meets, they'll be politely told they don't (and perhaps explain why). Still, there may be some aspects of clan culture that is still adhered to like the claims of sanctuary and embrace night parties. Given their own high ranks in Melee, Fortier and Edward Vignes might even have dueling as a mutual hobby.<br /> <br /> I think the Toreador might also avoid clan meetings. Not only is the clan distrusted because of the unique history of LA and the rule of Don Sebastian, Toreador salon culture is at the heart of the Camarilla. Much of their culture infuses the Camarilla and its expectations of proper social behavior. Meanwhile the Free States won't even call Disneyworld an Elysium, but simply a &quot;safety zone.&quot; LA Toreador who meet in salons and attempt to replicate the guilds, socials, and clan prestige are probably seen as people wanting to bring back all that is wrong with the hated Camarilla. Small, informal gatherings are probably OK. But I imagine LA Toreador wanting to do traditional Toreador things probably head out for an evening at the Vampire Club in San Francisco, and don't make a regular habit out of it.<br /> <br /> That leaves the Nosferatu, and I am of mixed minds here. First, I think it would be too tough for anyone to try to police the Nosferatu. So they hold their clan meetings. Having said that, I also think some anarchs might be worried. One reason is that the Justicar assigned the responsibility of combating the anarchs is the Nosferatu Justicar Petrodon. Another reason (though this is much less well known) is that the Nosferatu stick so much together than even Camarilla and Sabbat Nosferatu will exchange information! So it's likely the LA Nosferatu still share information with their Camarilla loyal brethren. While some sect loyalties will still be observed (there are plenty of NPC Nosferatu shown to be anarchs loyal to their cause), I imagine there are Camarilla loyal Nosferatu in LA that their anarch brethren do not snitch out. Whatever their political loyalties are individually, the Nosferatu are still loyal to their clan first (for various reasons).<br /> <br /> Last are the Caitiff. Of course there is no Caitiff clan culture, and I imagine most Caitiff have adjusted quite well in the system of &quot;gangs&quot;. However, this is not to say there is no prejudice against them. And for that reason I'll be introducing a group of Caitiff whose &quot;gang&quot; are all Caitiff and trying to organize the clanless together, in a manner similar to what Joseph Pander did in the Sabbat. There are no connections between the Sabbat Panders and these Caitiff, but I think the dynamics that compelled Pander in the Sabbat also applies here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  fixed typos 03-26-2025, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-25T12:47:56-07:00","id":1549564,"title":"","content":"I tend to agree that Clan has to be downplayed in LA, though one suspects that those Kindred players pursuing greater knowledge of Disciplines (Or seeking to be taken seriously outside the Free States) will have to know how to \u2018talk the talk\u2019 (and possibly toe the line) when it comes to Clan.<br /> <br /> While Clans are made up of individuals, in a setting and a \u2018splat\u2019 where all supernatural power stems from bloodline (and bloodlines often command more widespread respect than individual achievements), it\u2019s hard to deny their continuing influence over even the most defiantly Anarch individuals.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, my compliments on your analysis of the Clan situation - my only further suggestions is that the Clan Ventrue in LA might well be further splintered by the very different n personalities of the most prominent local members (I\u2019d bet money that Baron Fortier reminds Jesus Ramirez a little too much of his old boss and that neither of them is very included to trust a certain Camarilla defector or his \u2018Task Force Ex\u2019).<br /> <br /> It also seems highly, highly likely that the Countess d\u2019Audhemar would be working her tail off to mine the Toreador connection in Los Angeles for actionable intelligence (Though I suspect those Toreador still resident in the area would cut her dead should she go too far in the direction of actual recruitment).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-25T15:20:56-07:00","id":1549569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance?p=1549564#post1549564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, my compliments on your analysis of the Clan situation - my only further suggestions is that the Clan Ventrue in LA might well be further splintered by the very different n personalities of the most prominent local members</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine those three do their best not to hang out together for their own reasons.<br /> <br /> Also, I just reread Ramirez's profile, and it seems the other LA Kindred know little about him and assume he's the childe of Salvador Garcia. So it's likely nobody else even knows he's Ventrue. I assume Salvador knows but doesn't care at this point as the two are now best friends, and Salvador trusts him enough to run things on his behalf. So I'll just need to remember to tell PCs that he's Brujah until they learn otherwise (if ever).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T12:37:58-07:00","id":1550809,"title":"","content":"I saw another relevant bit in a reread of the Anarch Cookbook. As I've said multiple times on various posts, there's discrepancies between information earlier reported about the Free States in early sourcebooks like the Cookbook and Clanbook Brujah, and what we would get in the LABN sourcebook. I think this was likely deliberate possibly because the author of LABN didn't want to beholden to what was written before. As a result, STs wanting to run a Free State chronicle will need to decide how to handle this - choose one or the other, mix the two somehow, or something else? As for me, my approach is to try to integrate the two as best I can while ultimately deciding what to accept or reject.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the relevant section is called the Anarch Movement which in this book is the name by which the anarchs of the Free State govern themselves. The Movement only governs when there is a dispute. The contesting parties come before a council of their peers who are respected for their experience or power. This council is comprised of 3-5 anarchs. This council votes on the outcome. If one party disputes the outcome, they can appeal, but it is to the exact same council members. If it turns out any member or members voted unfairly, they get kicked off the council likely losing anarch status or even gaining a social Flaw like Notoriety. However, the section says that despite this method, most anarch disputes are handled by violence before any council is convened.<br /> <br /> Despite not being mentioned in LABN, this can easily be incorporated into it. A call for a council to arbitrate or mediate between parties is clearly something that can happen at a Rant. Presumably one or both sides ask for a council at a Rant, or possibly a third party asks the two sides to accept one. If both agree, 3-5 volunteers agree to arbitrate, possibly selected by the other attendees of the Rant. These anarchs are probably those who have slightly more anarch status than those possessed by the disputants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SX6x7DT4m4Q\" data-code=\"SX6x7DT4m4Q\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/SX6x7DT4m4Q/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Newly arrived, unproven, or uninvolved anarchs aren't going to get Jeremy MacNeil, Salvador Garcia, or Smiling Jack to appear on such a council. They'll probably get Kindred like Ariane or Steve Booth who only have Status 1. Kindred like MacNeil or Garcia would probably only join if one of the powerful barons get into a dispute, and both sides are looking for a way to end things peacefully but save face. It's a combination of which anarch volunteer to join such a council, and which ones are most acceptable to the Rant attendees.<br /> <br /> This probably requires the ST to determine better Status for many of the NPCs listed in LABN. There are examples of Status that does not make sense in my opinion. MacNeil has Status 5 which makes sense, but as he is a figure revered by anarchs throughout the world, it's probably more of a 6 or 7. Salvador Garcia, the author of the Anarch Manifesto and Status Perfectus, the acknowledged destroyer of Don Sebastian, leader/baron of La Hermandad, and active helper of anarchs in other domains only has Status 3. That's the same status as Amethyst and Edward Vignes who have no other claims to status than being barons (and in Vignes' case a rather minor one), and lower than Tara. I don't think that makes sense. Many characters have Status either lower or higher than I would expect. I recommend the ST adjust Status of canon NPCs so it makes sense to them.<br /> <br /> I'm sure certain anarchs are considered to render the best judgments and respected for their prowess. Some of these could regularly agree to join such councils. Others might be known to volunteer only rarely. In all cases, if the dispute seems stupid, petty, or resolution could be controversial, these anarchs might refuse to join to signify they don't want to become involved. Other ambitious anarchs might regularly volunteer, but not be accepted by the Rant because they have a low opinion of them. This could be a good way to distinguish these NPCs from one another, and how the greater anarch population sees them. <br /> <br /> For example, despite being respected barons, Geduld, Fortier, and Vignes might not volunteer since they know most Brujah might resent a decision coming from a Ventrue. Maybe you have a fairly minor anarch NPC who doesn't control any territory or lead a gang, but because he's well liked and respected is someone who frequently serves on councils for other low status anarchs. Maybe a respected baron volunteers to be on the arbitration council because he thinks the issue is important, or foresees more trouble down the line.<br /> <br /> Like with all decisions, enforcement depends on individual anarchs deciding to do that. I expected usually both sides accept the result whatever it is. If they wouldn't, why agree to an arbitration in the first place? But that may not be universal. So if one side refuses to accept the decision, it could be a paper outcome. However, someone who first agrees to arbitration and then refuses it when it does not go their way likely loses respect/status. It also might mean that some or all of the &quot;council&quot; might enforce the decision, especially if they consider the other side to be unfair or that their own reputations might suffer by someone denying their judgment. (Thus not only does one want anarchs on the council who is not only wise, but sufficiently strong to help enforce their decision). It might also convince some fence-sitters to come down on one side since there is now precedent of the community supporting the decision and political cover is provided.<br /> <br /> Disputes like the gang war in Anaheim probably has had other anarchs calling for arbitration, but because Tom Weaver and/or Alison Maller refuses, there is none and the violence continues.<br /> <br /> Such arbitration/mediation councils are a relatively minor thing, but I think it's a good way to distinguish how things are sometimes done in the Free States versus a domain with a prince. The first time PCs show up to a Rant, I'll likely show a request for arbitration and have an NPC explain what will happen. That way the concept is introduced. Because the term &quot;council&quot; gets used a lot for several different things in the Free States, I'll probably just have NPCs refer to this &quot;arbitration&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T13:20:12-07:00","id":1550855,"title":"","content":"This definitely sounds interesting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T12:54:27-07:00","id":1551629,"title":"","content":"Given the setting is LA and home to a tremendous celebrity culture, I wanted to do a post on Fame. I was not sure where to put it, but ultimately decided to do it here because Fame and celebrity will be a big impact on certain anarch activities. At some point, even anarchs will need to judge if certain celebrities are a threat to the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> The Fame background has always been part of character creation. It just makes hunting for blood easier, and by itself isn\u2019t necessarily any threat to the Masquerade. It just means more people want to be near you. Actual celebrity though invites attention from the media, and that is something else. As early as Chicago By Night 1e, it was said Baby Chorus (whose two frontmen only have Fame 2 each) would be considered a \u201cblatant violation\u201d of the Masquerade. Prince Lodin was even planning to hold a Conclave to judge the \u201ctransgressors of the Masquerade.\u201d (Lodin himself did not really seem to care about them, seeing it only as a pretext to call a Conclave so he could address other matters).<br /> <br /> So what about Kindred with even greater fame or celebrity? Normal character creation allows up to rank 5. Clanbook Toreador 1e had multiple templates with Fame 1 and 2, and one each for Fame 4 and 5 (the Horror Writer and Idol of Millions respectively). Both of those latter templates explicitly mention that other vampires fear they jeopardize the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> The LABN sourcebook strangely does not have any NPCs with Fame greater than 1 despite being in the film and television capital of the world and home to a huge music and media industry. In contrast, Annabelle Triabelle of Chicago has Fame 4 due to her mask as \u201cEllen Stanley-Greer,\u201d the socialite wife of a newspaper syndicate baron. (Presumably Annabelle is a case where Fame does not necessarily link to a Masquerade breach because despite a certain prominence, most people would not recognize her and journalist and popular interest in her is rather low.) I would suggest that perhaps Annabelle\u2019s description and rank of Fame does not exactly tie in together, but there\u2019s always been a lot of that in sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> LABN even mentions that the venue A Taste of LA has hosted several \u201cfairly well-known\u201d Kindred bands and name dropped the aforementioned Baby Chorus and two new bands, \u201cTopaz Jet\u201d and the \u201cnow-defunct Vital Signs.\u201d (The name dropping of Baby Chorus ignores Chicago By Night\u2019s statement that Baby Chorus was only known in Chicago and the surrounding region.)<br /> <br /> However, I think the vast majority of players would expect that in any chronicle set in LA there would be multiple vampires of extremely high Fame and celebrity. Vampires who are movie celebrities, music video icons, and other paparazzi targets. I want to give that to them, but I want to work out and explore such concepts and the consequences of them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-13T03:42:54-07:00","id":1551650,"title":"","content":"Well in all fairness it\u2019s perfectly possible for Baby Chorus to go from \u2018local heroes\u2019 to \u2018best kept secret\u2019 in terms of national fame - I.E. they\u2019re not a mainstream hit, but to those in the know they\u2019re The Guys (Equivalent to a movie becoming a Cult Classic, perhaps?).<br /> <br /> It also bears pointing out that in the nature of things there aren\u2019t going to be very many Kindred bands, so those who DO exist might well get some very handsome offers for live gigs coming in from some fair-flung places (If only because it\u2019s much easier to enjoy a party when you don\u2019t have to worry about breaching the Masquerade in front of the entertainment).<br /> <br /> Also, I love the name \u2018Vital Signs\u2019and having sone fun trying to puzzle out what they and \u2018Topaz Jet\u2019 might sounds like (My basic notion is that the former are more PUNK, the latter are more Gothic, but that both put the Rock &amp; Roll into GothicPunk).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-13T04:11:32-07:00","id":1551651,"title":"","content":"Regarding Fame in Kindred, I have two major notions:-<br /> <br /> - Firstly, that for a vampire being famous is a double edged sword at best: even when you\u2019re not famous for being a vampire, enjoying the sort of fame that consistently attracts (or worse yet COMMANDS) attention is generally unhelpful when one is obliged to live a lifestyle uncomfortably like that of a serial killer or a mobster or a double agent.<br /> <br /> After all \u2018Famous Serial Killer\u2019, \u2018Famous Gangster\u2019 or \u2018Famous Spy\u2019 are generally synonyms for \u2018They got caught\u2019 (and if a vampire gets caught, Kindred or Cainite, Bad Things happen \u2026 and not just to their captors).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Secondly, I think it therefore makes sense to grade \u2018Fame\u2019 on a curve when it comes to vampires: for one thing, I feel that if a person is famous and celebrated, in the prime of their pomp and prosperity, they are extremely unlikely to become a vampire (Even at the end of their life) because they already have it made, so why upset the applecart?<br /> <br /> It also bears pointing out that famous and successful people are surrounded by potential eyewitnesses (Heck, by multiple circles of eyewitnesses), so even if the target is willing to go from the top of the ladder to the very rattle of the snake, it\u2019s difficult to believe that most vampires would be able to avoid scrutiny for long enough to kill the subject and raise them from the dead without the deceased being noticed.<br /> <br /> <br /> (I may have noted this before, but I tend to feel that a solid majority of Kindred claiming to be Charlemagne or Frederick Barbarossa are either fooling themselves or lying to everyone: honestly, Heinrich Himmler is one of the more plausible high-profile recruits to the undead because that dude was on the run, out of options and quite literally suicidally desperate).<br /> <br /> <br /> Or, put another way, a vampire who enjoys Fame as a mortal must either be willing or downright eager to trade in the whole blessed lot if they want to become a successful vampire - because successful vampires attract very few eyewitnesses and leave even fewer in a talkative state of mind, especially over the long term.<br /> <br /> Now this process of shedding their fame isn\u2019t always instantaneous (With the obvious exception of a Nosferatu \u2019Cleopatra\u2019, a Sabbat \u2018shovelhead\u2019 and presumably one ir two other exception) but sooner or later a Famous vampire is going to have to shed their mortal fame if they want to outlive their first generation (No matter how obscure their place of residence).<br /> <br /> <br /> That came out a little more tangled than I meant it to: in a nutshell what I mean is that a vampire who enjoyed celebrity in their breathing days will have to give up that Fame sooner or later; a vampire who acquired some measure of Fame after the Embrace is, by definition, going to live a lifestyle too weird to achieve more than niche fame amongst mortals (Especially when the Masquerade is firmly in place); and it seems unlikely to me that extremely famous and celebrated people are going to make attractive recruitment prospects for the undead in the first place, because to my mind those who do Best as vampires are those who can work the system, but are willing to live outside it, mostly in obscurity (A profile that definitely does not cover major celebrities in any field).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-13T04:27:47-07:00","id":1551652,"title":"","content":"Something I forgot to add - does \u2018Fame\u2019 mean \u2018Vampire famous\u2019 (Grading on that curve I mentioned) or \u2018Famous period\u2019? (In the sense that humans and vampires will have a a little bit of \u2018whoa, it\u2019s that guy!\u2019).<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, to get back to the main point, I think that it makes perfect sense for LA BY NIGHT to have relatively few vampires who are Famous-famous (As opposed to \u2018vampire Famous\u2019) because Los Angeles is one of the worst places in the world for a vampire to remain Famous - given that as one of THE major media hubs on the planet, if you\u2019re very famous then the media will not only take an interest, they will STALK you: they will take an interest (Not necessarily a friendly interest) in every little thing about you and put it up where the whole world can not only see, but where the whole world will actually take a close interest.<br /> <br /> Heck, this applies even when a vampire wasn\u2019t very famous to start with or mostly tries to lie low, because so much of LA is bound up with industries that draw attention from the media even when nobody especially famous is in the vicinity - and sustained scrutiny, however casual, is something most Kindred can\u2019t sustain for very long.<br /> <br /> <br /> Add that sheer intensity of interest to the fairly casual organisation of the Free States (They want to maintain the Masquerade, but I suspect most Anarchs are reluctant to pursue the sort of inglorious clean-up jobs and outright resistant to the constraints that the Camarilla are fully prepared to insist upon, with unhappy consequences to those that ignore them) and I suspect that those Kindred who get too famous in the Free States will either be invited or positively obliged to do elsewhere - possibly all the way to Hell, if they get a little too big for their britches.<br /> <br /> Anarchs enjoy their iconoclasm, but they\u2019re not above some Tall Poppy syndrome in pursuit of their own self-interests (and as their preferred alternative to embracing the sort of quiet afterlife, full of constraints, the Camarilla insist upon).<br /> <br /> Put another way, in LA a little fame is winked at, too much Fame will attract something other than admiration\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-13T14:43:38-07:00","id":1551663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance?p=1551650#post1551650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also bears pointing out that in the nature of things there aren\u2019t going to be very many Kindred bands, so those who DO exist might well get some very handsome offers for live gigs coming in from some fair-flung places (If only because it\u2019s much easier to enjoy a party when you don\u2019t have to worry about breaching the Masquerade in front of the entertainment).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a valid point. However, a Baby Chorus band tour from Chicago to LA and back would likely be very hazardous for the band, and they'd have a lot of questions to answer about their stay in LA. I'm much more inclined to have any vampire (or ghoul) musicians that play in LA to be locally based and have easy access to the city. I have a few in mind. However, I should come up with some story on who Vital Signs were and how they became defunct, as well as create something for Topaz Jet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance?p=1551650#post1551650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Fame in Kindred,</div> </div> </div> </div>All good comments. The Embrace will bring both good and bad things to any celebrity (especially one in their prime), and a lot of individual factors will determine if the celebrity will adapt well or if it'll be some kind of disaster best avoided. Someone whose career has already peaked or has has noticed some kind of physical decline they deeply want to avoid would be better candidates than someone who thinks their career or life is only going to get better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance?p=1551650#post1551650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sooner or later a Famous vampire is going to have to shed their mortal fame if they want to outlive their first generation (No matter how obscure their place of residence).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very true. Fame (or celebrity) can only last for so long. Sooner or later all vampires with Fame/celebrity will need to drop out of the public focus and reinvent their mortal mask. Of course, such timelines are usually out of scope for the length of any chronicle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance?p=1551650#post1551650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I forgot to add - does \u2018Fame\u2019 mean \u2018Vampire famous\u2019</div> </div> </div> </div>I would consider the Fame background to be solely of use among mortals and have no correspondence to vampire society (although of course anyone with Fame is just as likely to be known to exist among vampires as it is among the mortal public as long as the vampire pays any attention to mortal society).<br /> <br /> Being well known among the Kindred is probably a function of Status, age, sect, and deed that would be well known among the Kindred.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance?p=1551650#post1551650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, to get back to the main point, I think that it makes perfect sense for LA BY NIGHT to have relatively few vampires who are Famous-famous (As opposed to \u2018vampire Famous\u2019) because Los Angeles is one of the worst places in the world for a vampire to remain Famous - given that as one of THE major media hubs on the planet, if you\u2019re very famous then the media will not only take an interest, they will STALK you: they will take an interest (Not necessarily a friendly interest) in every little thing about you and put it up where the whole world can not only see, but where the whole world will actually take a close interest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. However, I think this is something that would be fun to play out in a chronicle. Have that Idol of Millions Toreador template character exist. Interact with the PCs. Have them see all the good that comes with it, and then eventually all the problems it causes. Have them make the decision to take that character out right before the whole thing blows up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance?p=1551650#post1551650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anarchs enjoy their iconoclasm, but they\u2019re not above some Tall Poppy syndrome in pursuit of their own self-interests (and as their preferred alternative to embracing the sort of quiet afterlife, full of constraints, the Camarilla insist upon).<br /> <br /> Put another way, in LA a little fame is winked at, too much Fame will attract something other than admiration\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Having a mix of different Fame levels and celebrity types would be good in the sense the PCs can see how different levels and types play out in both the mortal and Kindred worlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-13T14:55:06-07:00","id":1551664,"title":"","content":"The most common celebrity Kindred character concept is likely that of the musician. It\u2019s easy to justify the Fame background, and as a career it\u2019s one which someone who is only active at night can probably handle. There may be some difficulty with rehearsals, recordings, shows, and promotions, but not enough that they can\u2019t be addressed and dismissed by the ST and players.<br /> <br /> Famous models can also be easily done (the nineties was the high of the \u201csupermodel\u201d). If you are successful enough, you can probably get away with a restricted (nocturnal) activity cycle because other people are more desperate to get you than you are for a job. (Less famous models would find their career dead unless they can quickly achieve fame through Presence and the like.) Or the model just goes into early retirement and adjusts to \u201cfamous for being famous.\u201d<br /> <br /> Actual film and television celebrities probably have their career ended. Too much money is at stake, and too many people are involved for even prima donnas to demand that they only appear and perform at night. Acting exceptions may apply if the performer begins doing odd independent movies that they can completely control, or if they transition to a local theatre performance. Such odd career choices may provide some satisfaction or even acclaim, but effectively they\u2019ve now become former film and television actors. They may still have Fame and have paparazzi follow them, but their career in Hollywood is dead. This could cause some bitterness unless they really like being a vampire and are good with the exchange, or had already decided they wanted out of the biz.<br /> <br /> There will also be certain executives, producers, and other business end types that technically count as celebrities in Tinseltown. They\u2019ll be important people that Variety and other industry press will report on. LA is an industry town after all even if such people aren\u2019t \u201cfamous\u201d elsewhere. If they\u2019re rich and powerful enough, they may not technically hold a day office job. They just make things happen and then show up to the award shows at night.<br /> <br /> Any \u201cretired\u201d celebrities could also work as vampire character concepts. They could be older actors and musicians, \u201cdisgraced\u201d creative types or those with reputations as difficult to work with and thus forcibly retired, or still relatively young sports atheletes who have already passed their pinnacle or perhaps been injured. (I\u2019m sure there are lots of other examples that could be used.)<br /> <br /> Los Angeles has all the major professional sports leagues (including multiple teams in the same league), lots of minor league times, is a center for many action sports, is home to lots of retired athletes including non-team sports, and has many sports venues used to host special events. Vampire professional athlete is not a usual vampire character, but it\u2019s just as valid as many other celebrity concepts. Retired athletes tend to still be fairly young and near their prime and don\u2019t need a day job anymore. Plus lots of reasons why they might enjoy being a vampire (fear of aging and physical decline, wanting to compensate for a disability, having blown all the money they made and wanting a way they can still enjoy existence).<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also what I call the fake celebrity or entourage celebrity. They\u2019re the people around the talent. The general public might not know who they are, but the entertainment industry people recognize them, they enjoy a lot of the same benefits as their celebrity friend, they provide a means for others to access the true celebrity so they\u2019re sought be others, and they can become notorious on their own in the right circles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IhrAAfNbw0I\" data-code=\"IhrAAfNbw0I\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/IhrAAfNbw0I/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> (I wish I could find a better video of Gob Bluth as \u201cGetaway\u201d when he was hanging around Mark Cherry in the series Arrested Development. I am very tempted to create a character based on him for the chronicle. He\u2019s such a parasite he\u2019d be the perfect basis for a character.)<br /> <br /> Today there\u2019s also influencers and YouTube celebrities, but of course they didn\u2019t exist back when the sourcebook came out. All we had was public-access television.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-15T13:50:23-07:00","id":1551684,"title":"","content":"So what does this mean for the Free States?<br /> <br /> Well, it means some of these celebrities might not be able to leave southern California. They run the risk some Justicar or archon may do something. Of course, their celebrity might also protect them as harming them might cause more trouble than what it is worth (because of the ensuing media attention and law enforcement investigation).<br /> <br /> However, it could also mean the opposite in that if they behave and follow the rules, maybe Princes might welcome them as part of making sure the Masquerade is strengthened. Or there is a greater chance they might be offered benefits in exchange for spying or doing some errand for the Justicars. After all, how many of these top vampire celebrities who just happened to be embraced in the Free States want to be able to visit wherever they liked just as they did when they were mortal? For that reason, embracing these highly privileged, rich, famous celebrities might be seen as a security risk by some anarchs.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also the possibility that celebrity vampires embraced elsewhere who do run afoul of some local Prince (maybe for Masquerade reasons) seek refuge in Los Angeles.<br /> <br /> Also, if celebrity vampires screw up in LA and breach the Masquerade, those breaches still need to be cleaned up and the violator perhaps eliminated. The Status Perfectus still maintains the need for a Masquerade after all. A certain number of celebrity \u201coverdose\u201d deaths, \u201csuicides\u201d, decapitating \u201caccidents\u201d, and other tragic demises might be the result of vampire celebrities being eliminated for their crimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-17T20:35:26-07:00","id":1551750,"title":"","content":"What might it mean for Petrodon?<br /> <br /> LA celebrity vampires are a threat to be managed, but if possible turned to the Camarilla\u2019s benefit. Many celebrities would want the ability to travel elsewhere on occasion, and many would welcome a more stable (and therefore safe) environment than the chaos and violence often found in the Free States. The potential for double agents, spies, and so on is not insignificant. (It is also not inevitable as there are plausible reasons why some celebrity vampires would prefer the Free States over the Camarilla.)<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also evidence that suggests at some point the issue of celebrity and the Masquerade will be addressed by a conclave. After debate and deliberation, some blanket policy will dictate how the Camarilla will handle such \u201cthreats\u201d including destruction of such vampires (or at least how the Justicar who called that conclave will do). This would have very potential big impact on such celebrity vampires in the Free States. I\u2019m thinking that might be a very good story idea to introduce at some point in the chronicle. Perhaps the PCs and certain NPCs might attend such a conclave.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-19T13:35:59-07:00","id":1551773,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to pop in and suggest some notions for Vital Signs and Topaz Jet that occurred to me - my knowledge of the LA musical scene is sufficiently shaky for me to regard these as especially sketchy sketches, but hopefully there will be enough to go on with.<br /> <br /> <br /> VITAL SIGNS - A name that has \u2018Rock and Roll band that just keeps rolling like the Stones\u2019 written all over it, so let\u2019s imagine that long term admirers of the band are entirely convinced that it\u2019s not so much that the band has broken beyond all repair, it\u2019s that they\u2019ve hit the \u2018break up\u2019 phase of their break up/make up cycle (Possibly with an eye to coming back as their own grown-up sons after a suitable interlude).<br /> <br /> - Members Tom, Rick and Harry are all creations of the same Sire (Tradition suggests a Toreador, but I like the idea that their boss/manager/vampire dad is a Ventrue who decided that his way of graduating from the agoge with honours would involve making the LA music industry his personal preserve: as he\u2019s a Ventrue working his way very carefully through a whole thicket of thorny Toreador complicated by watchful Anarchs, this process is taking longer than hoped, henchmen or no henchmen).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Mental image of their being roughly the same age by the calendar, but embraced separately (Mostly as a reward for being moderately useful henchmen and superbly useful cover, because Rockstars can get away with an amazing amount of weirdness and criminality, petty or otherwise) so that one is forever twenty something, another middle aged and the last \u2026 well nobody\u2019s quite sure because that dude was frickin\u2019 ageless even before he was a vampire, if only because he NEVER looked young.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Being allowed to remain a band is, of course, their incentive to do what the Boss tells them when the whole Anarch Free States say that they are in no way obliged to do so (Why do they want to be a band? \u201cGroupies!\u201d \u201cThe music, dude\u201d \u201cIt was either that or get a real job\u201d).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Nevertheless in addition to the usual clashes of artistic temperament, the lads are currently being pulled away from each other by the fact that Harry is so hungry to be THE rockstar he might shatter the Masquerade if he only he had the nerve, while Rick is more eager to advance himself as a vampire thsn a musician and Tom just wants to play his music, dudes, chill and let\u2019s just be Rock n\u2019Roll vampires.<br /> <br /> Y\u2019know, when the Boss doesn\u2019t need us to be gangsters.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Mental image of Vital Signs, musically speaking, being a no-frills, hard-driving rock and roll band with more than a hint of punk: in terms of sartorial style they tend to Go Big and change by the whim, not least because it\u2019s<br /> much easier to avoid people noticing you don\u2019t age when everything else about you changes by the Fashion season.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Topaz Jet I have a less vivid mental image of, but I tend to imagine them as a pair of singers (calling themselves \u2018Topaz\u2019 and \u2018Jet\u2019 of course) who were turned by a pair of vampires - representing two clans - who were somewhat interested in seeing whether this would pull a close team apart over the long term, but far more interested in sealing a covenant with a shared business endeavour.<br /> <br /> The ladies themselves, of course, were coming of age when their chances of becoming more than backup were clearly visible, but far enough in the future that they had serious concerns they\u2019d be too old to seize the day when their Big Opportunity came (At least by the standards of the LA music industry): offered the chance to be eternally young at the price of fheir managers becoming their owner-proprietors, the future Topaz and Jet seized their opportunity and (some decades later) are finally in a position to be the Bug Stars they\u2019ve always wanted to be.<br /> <br /> Now if only they didn\u2019t have to be POP STARS to get there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-20T12:59:02-07:00","id":1551789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance?p=1551773#post1551773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wanted to pop in and suggest some notions for Vital Signs and Topaz Jet that occurred to me - my knowledge of the LA musical scene is sufficiently shaky for me to regard these as especially sketchy sketches, but hopefully there will be enough to go on with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are some interesting ideas and certainly builds on the information provided in LABN. My problem is that in terms of NPCs, I already have something like 6 NPC musicians and adding five more bumps that number to 11. That's a lot of similar musician concepts. Even for LA, that may be a bit too many vampire musicians. And I haven't even begun to add other NPCs that would cover other types of celebrity fame.<br /> <br /> I originally had 3 NPCs of my own based on pre-existing characters my players would recognize, and I want to keep them. Another two are filler characters based on the Fake Rapper and Gangster Rapper templates in the original Brujah Clanbook. As filler characters, I can easily jettison them or add them as &quot;new&quot; vampires later on. The last was Delilah Monroe from the Chaos Factor sourcebook. I could easily replace her as I already have someone who is representative of the SoCal punk music scene, but I really like the idea of including an actual canon NPC and do something with her. Having two SoCal punk musicians isn't bad for me because I have very different plans for these characters, and one of my players is into punk music and can contribute a lot to the setting there.<br /> <br /> I was originally just planning on having all the members of the &quot;now defunct&quot; Vital Signs be destroyed. However, I really like your idea of the band as a &quot;break up/make up&quot; type band that was wildly popular. Rather than have them be native to LA, I'm considering going full &quot;Rolling Stones&quot; and making them part of the British Invasion (perhaps somewhere between the Stones and the Animals in terms of popularity) and already being in their forties by the time they were embraced (and thus having lots of complications from previous marriages, children, etc.). They would have been embraced in London (perhaps by <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lianna_(Leanan)\" target=\"_blank\">Lianna</a> in World of Darkness 1e). Their sire would be notorious in musical circles as one of those women who somehow ruined the band (explaining why they broke up the last time). <br /> <br /> They were subsequently chased out of London because of Masquerade issues and went to LA because it was really the best place for them to be safe. They'd be powerful enough in the music industry that if they still wanted to produce albums they could - nobody is going to tell them they cannot come in only at night. And they could easily play single night gigs in SoCal and get everyone excited they might be getting back together. Having such a worldwide popular band would address a lot of issues concerning Fame. Although there may only be three now, perhaps there were a fourth or even a fifth before those were destroyed (always described as some tragic death appropriate for such hard rocking musicians like an overdose).<br /> <br /> Just to reduce the number of musician characters, I may just have Topaz Jet be the name of Delilah's band and throw some of the other existing characters into it. It doesn't need to be any of their main bands, just a side project they employ when they want to play locally for a Kindred audience.<br /> <br /> There are no right or wrong answers here. STs just need to figure out what works best for their chronicles and which canonical elements they want to employ or not.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-23T10:24:04-07:00","id":1551824,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, glad you like some<br /> of my notions for \u2018VS\u2019 (You can bet that so many, many puns have been crafted to lampoon the band\u2019s effort to be become known as \u2018The Signs\u2019, many of them ending up as tabloid headlines).<br /> <br /> I like your idea of making VS a \u2018British Invasion\u2019 band, though it amuses to imagine that it took them until the Stones started gathering a little moss to <i>really</i> get going - mostly because they seemed to be aging better than their peers (I mean those who actually bothered aging at all, not Keith Richards).<br /> <br /> One also likes your idea of their Sire being female, though I\u2019m still fond of my own notion that the band weren\u2019t embraced all at once but brought over by stages (With one embraced in the 1960s/1970s to keep him from joining the \u201827 club\u2019 as the price of the band becoming a front for an elder vampire\u2019s wandering, then the others being brought over as and when they proved themselves sufficiently useful idiots and/or became sufficiently treasures pets), if only because having every single member of a band stop aging at exactly the same time would be tricky to explain (Especially before the invention of Botox).<br /> <br /> There will, of course, be a whole soap opera of interpersonal shenanigans making the process much, much messier than the straightforward account up these makes it sound.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I\u2019m not going to lie, mental images of Fake Rapper and Gangster Rapper having absolutely no bad blood between them - because Gangster Rapper is NOT going to enable that pretender mothersucker\u2019s career by showing him the slightest hint of interest - amuses me.<br /> <br /> Especially if the two of them are obliged to share the same recording studio (Though to date never at the same time).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-23T10:27:59-07:00","id":1551825,"title":"","content":"Also, this may sound completely stupid but I absolutely love the notion of Vital Signs having bumped into (or otherwise got wind of) the enigmatic Dark Selina at some point.<br /> <br /> This is for no other reason than that \u2018Dark Selina\u2019 is absolutely a name that belongs in a Rock album.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-23T17:46:17-07:00","id":1551831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance?p=1551824#post1551824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One also likes your idea of their Sire being female, though I\u2019m still fond of my own notion that the band weren\u2019t embraced all at once but brought over by stages (With one embraced in the 1960s/1970s to keep him from joining the \u201827 club\u2019 as the price of the band becoming a front for an elder vampire\u2019s wandering, then the others being brought over as and when they proved themselves sufficiently useful idiots and/or became sufficiently treasures pets), if only because having every single member of a band stop aging at exactly the same time would be tricky to explain (Especially before the invention of Botox).</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine the band members should be embraced in stages if only because it is exceedingly unlikely any vampire could obtain permission to sire three to five childer at once. As a 350 year old elder who travels a lot though, Lianna could conceivably obtain permission to sire from multiple princes.<br /> <br /> As a carousing seductress, she could have simply determined that the members of Vital Signs knew how to party and attached herself to them as their favorite groupie. (Her artistic skills aren't that high, but she has tremendous Style, Empathy, and Carousing.) She could have easily controlled them as a vampire for a long time. Once the band was big enough to have their own chartered jets, she could even tour with them without fear of daylight. Embrace one in London. Another in southern France once they're tax exiles. One more in LA because she doesn't need permission. Any other city where some Prince owes her something.<br /> <br /> In fact the games she plays between them and when she embraced each one is probably the secret story behind every &quot;break up&quot;.<br /> <br /> Of course, simply because you get permission to legally embrace someone does not mean every domain wants to welcome a bunch of new vampires that are coming &quot;home&quot; with Lianna. Or that towards the end every time they toured, Princes wanted to deal with the issue of accommodating so many new vampires (although the band itself probably has an immense Herd they could call upon, and would have learned early on from Lianna how to handle them in a way that does not risk the Masquerade). Lots of reasons for resentment against them and why they'd eventually need to relocate to LA. (Their sire of course got off scott free, but maybe she'll come to visit them.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-25T14:06:39-07:00","id":1551865,"title":"","content":"I feel rather guilty for producing such a clear image of Vital Signs, whilst rather neglecting Topaz Jet, but a number of possible names for singles or albums by VS occurred to me and I therefore share them with you:-<br /> <br /> - Shock Treatment<br /> - Cut &amp; Run<br /> - Bedlam Daze<br /> - Skin &amp; Bone<br /> - Stroke of Genius<br /> - Jugular Vain (They absolutely insist that spelling was deliberate, honest)<br /> - Kiss of Life<br /> - Eye of the Needle (\u201cDRUGS ARE BAD, now please excuse us while we rock them anyway\u201d)<br /> - The Strange Case of Doctor Devil and Sister Hide<br /> - The Cabinet of Doctor Death<br /> - Brain Waves (Record cover WILL show somebody waving with a human wave in their hand \u2026 possibly while surfing)<br /> <br /> What do you mean \u201cBlatantly obvious to the point of being lazy?\u201d (Next thing you\u2019ll be suggesting they <i>watched</i> the sequel to THE ROCKY HORROR PICTURE SHOW before ripping off the title).<br /> <br /> I mean SPOOKY TOOTH put out an album called \u201cWolf at the Door\u2019 for crying out loud! (Of course they did, stands to reason, wonderful lads the \u2018Tooth, Vital Signs are absolutely delighted nobody important got killed that one time).<br /> <br /> <br /> In the interests of balancing things out a bit, here are a few faltering attempts at a shortlist of Topaz Jet titles (Singles or album):-<br /> <br /> - Burn Billy Burn<br /> - Hotshot<br /> - Diamond Dance 2000<br /> - Bling Ding Ring<br /> - 24 Carat Killer<br /> - Nightshade Baby<br /> - Fresh from the Pit<br /> - Ruby delight<br /> - Ring out (\u201cRing out Ring out, Ring out ring out\u201d)<br /> - Tourmaline Dream","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}